## Trading Style: What High Volume Really Means

The High Volume archetype tag assigned to Katello reveals a specific approach to prediction markets. High-volume traders typically share several characteristics that distinguish them from more passive participants. They tend to be active across multiple markets simultaneously, they often trade into and out of positions rather than simply holding to resolution, and they deploy capital at a scale that requires genuine conviction in their probability assessments. For Katello, the combination of 33 markets traded and over $4.6 million in total volume suggests an average position size that is substantial by Polymarket standards. This is not a trader dabbling with small experimental bets. The high-volume approach also implies that Katello likely captures opportunities from price movements before resolution, taking profits when markets shift in favorable directions rather than waiting for final outcomes in every case.

